WEBVTT

00:02.900 --> 00:04.740
A long, long time ago.

00:04.960 --> 00:07.640
A story from about a hundred years ago.

00:08.530 --> 00:13.640
Nadja, guided by destiny, arrived in Switzerland.

00:17.850 --> 00:19.140
NAAJA

00:17.850 --> 00:19.140
Nadja,

00:19.270 --> 00:21.810
With your eyes

00:19.270 --> 00:21.810
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:21.810 --> 00:23.020
Nadja,

00:21.810 --> 00:23.020
NAAJA

00:23.060 --> 00:25.320
What do you see?

00:23.060 --> 00:25.320
Nani ga mieru

00:25.360 --> 00:28.240
Shining in the far distance,

00:25.360 --> 00:28.240
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:28.240 --> 00:30.610
The door to the future,

00:28.240 --> 00:30.610
Mirai no tobira

00:31.530 --> 00:34.990
That's what I'm searching for

00:31.530 --> 00:34.990
Sagashite iru

00:34.990 --> 00:42.210
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:42.920 --> 00:46.420
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:42.920 --> 00:46.420
Minna egao de aetara

00:46.500 --> 00:49.760
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:46.500 --> 00:49.760
Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:49.800 --> 00:53.010
It could be so much more fun

00:49.800 --> 00:53.010
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

00:53.050 --> 00:56.470
The world is wide, but it's still one

00:53.050 --> 00:56.470
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

00:56.850 --> 01:00.140
I can't see the end of the journey

00:56.850 --> 01:00.140
Tabi no owari wa mienai

01:00.270 --> 01:03.600
God is the only one who could possibly know

01:00.270 --> 01:03.600
Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:03.770 --> 01:07.360
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:03.770 --> 01:07.360
Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:07.400 --> 01:09.530
I will go waving

01:07.400 --> 01:09.530
Te wo furinagara

01:09.610 --> 01:16.280
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:09.610 --> 01:16.280
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:16.330 --> 01:19.040
But I won't look back

01:16.330 --> 01:19.040
Ushiro mukanai

01:19.370 --> 01:24.330
Until the day my dream comes true

01:19.370 --> 01:24.330
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:24.630 --> 01:28.050
Nadja, Your smile

01:24.630 --> 01:28.050
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:28.130 --> 01:31.470
Nadja, gives me courage

01:28.130 --> 01:31.470
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:31.510 --> 01:34.430
Under the blue sky,

01:31.510 --> 01:34.430
Aoi sora no shita de

01:34.550 --> 01:37.390
I will find the place

01:34.550 --> 01:37.390
Ashita no yukue

01:37.680 --> 01:41.600
where my future lies

01:37.680 --> 01:41.600
Mitsukeru kara

01:55.590 --> 01:56.130
﻿It's finished!

01:56.800 --> 01:57.840
﻿Look, look!

01:58.760 --> 01:59.390
﻿Here!

02:03.140 --> 02:05.060
﻿What a beautiful sight...

02:06.650 --> 02:09.360
﻿No matter how many times I come here, Switzerland is still beautiful.

02:10.610 --> 02:11.530
﻿Master!

02:11.730 --> 02:13.650
﻿Where are we headed?

02:13.650 --> 02:16.070
﻿Right. We're headed to the Le Man Orphanage.

02:16.910 --> 02:18.070
﻿An orphanage?

02:18.240 --> 02:19.870
﻿There, we're going to put on a charity performance for the kids.

02:20.200 --> 02:23.120
﻿Charity, you say? That means we don't get paid, right?

02:23.370 --> 02:25.580
﻿It's unusual, for you to work for free!

02:26.250 --> 02:29.250
﻿I could never take money from the darling little children...

02:28.360 --> 02:30.570
They helped us once before.

02:31.800 --> 02:34.340
﻿When the car broke down, they let us stay the night, you see...

02:34.840 --> 02:37.760
﻿Since then, whenever we're in the area, we stop by.

02:38.140 --> 02:39.720
﻿So that's why...

02:40.410 --> 02:42.700
I don't like that tone of voice!

02:42.700 --> 02:44.040
Yeah~?

02:43.810 --> 02:45.060
﻿The Le Man Orphanage...

02:45.040 --> 02:46.290
Stop, you!

02:46.870 --> 02:49.750
I knew it was something like that!

02:46.980 --> 02:48.520
﻿I wonder what kind of place it is?

02:51.440 --> 02:53.070
﻿It's started to blow...

02:53.400 --> 02:55.320
﻿The winds of destiny...

03:00.780 --> 03:02.620
﻿We will be at the Le Man Orphanage soon.

03:04.250 --> 03:05.000
﻿Yes.

03:10.400 --> 03:15.400
Francis In the Morning Light

03:17.720 --> 03:20.140
﻿It's beautiful now.

03:20.470 --> 03:22.180
It's a ﻿wonderful library.

03:35.740 --> 03:37.780
﻿We're finally back after all this time!

03:37.780 --> 03:39.700
﻿The Dandelion Troupe!

03:39.780 --> 03:44.200
﻿A fantastical time filled with love and hope is about to start now!

03:52.500 --> 03:54.000
﻿Our rookie dancer from the sky...

03:54.000 --> 03:57.340
﻿Lady Nadja will dance a Tyrolean dance...

03:57.720 --> 03:59.800
﻿Take a look!

04:19.150 --> 04:20.610
﻿Let's all dance together!

04:33.790 --> 04:35.500
﻿We have been looking forward to your visit!

04:35.750 --> 04:37.670
﻿It's been a long time, madam director.

04:38.960 --> 04:40.670
How do you like the library?

04:40.680 --> 04:42.590
﻿Everyone is very happy with it.

05:03.360 --> 05:04.490
﻿Francis!

05:06.780 --> 05:07.620
﻿Nadja...!

05:09.120 --> 05:10.620
﻿Let's dance some more!

05:10.620 --> 05:12.250
﻿Please?

05:13.460 --> 05:14.620
﻿Nadja?

05:16.840 --> 05:19.000
﻿Madam director! You're looking good!

05:19.300 --> 05:20.880
﻿And, you as well.

05:21.420 --> 05:22.670
﻿Hm? A guest?

05:23.130 --> 05:25.140
﻿Ahh. Let me introduce you.

05:25.850 --> 05:27.550
﻿This gentleman is from England...

05:28.390 --> 05:30.220
﻿I'm Francis Harcourt.

05:31.060 --> 05:32.230
﻿Francis...

05:32.730 --> 05:35.190
﻿Harcourt? From that ducal house?

05:39.110 --> 05:42.820
﻿Due to his fund raising, we have received many donations.

05:43.070 --> 05:45.530
﻿And, we were able to build this wonderful library.

05:46.120 --> 05:47.990
﻿Let us all thank him.

05:48.450 --> 05:51.910
﻿Mr. Francis, Thank You Very Much!

05:54.920 --> 05:56.790
﻿Um... this is for you...

05:58.210 --> 05:59.210
﻿Thank you.

06:02.050 --> 06:02.920
﻿Everyone..

06:03.720 --> 06:06.090
﻿A book has many things in it.

06:06.970 --> 06:09.800
﻿There's knowledge, of course, but also feelings.

06:10.180 --> 06:11.680
﻿I hope you read many books..

06:11.680 --> 06:13.980
﻿...and foster a generous heart in yourselves.

06:18.610 --> 06:20.400
﻿You must be tired from a long journey.

06:20.610 --> 06:22.730
We've ﻿prepared a room upstairs for you.

06:23.530 --> 06:24.740
﻿Thank you very much.

06:27.530 --> 06:28.740
﻿Nadja, look!

06:32.160 --> 06:34.200
﻿There's a book called "The Way of the Warrior"!

06:34.210 --> 06:35.750
﻿Oh! About samurai?

06:35.810 --> 06:36.900
Yeah, that's right!

06:37.600 --> 06:38.860
Let me see it, too!

06:38.210 --> 06:39.460
﻿Please, come this way.

06:39.460 --> 06:40.690
I was looking at it first!

06:40.250 --> 06:41.000
﻿Yes.

06:40.690 --> 06:41.270
Dont' be stingy!

06:41.270 --> 06:42.320
Give it!

06:42.320 --> 06:43.280
I don't want to!

06:43.280 --> 06:45.030
Let go!

06:44.340 --> 06:45.550
﻿Stop getting in my way!

06:45.670 --> 06:47.780
﻿Hey, Master! You're acting like a kid!

06:47.380 --> 06:49.200
I'm the Troupe Master!

06:47.780 --> 06:49.280
Ahh! Geez! Stop it!

06:49.280 --> 06:49.550
You don't know when to give up, do you!

06:49.550 --> 06:51.680
﻿Humph! Ahh! Darn it!
You don't know when to give up, do you

06:51.680 --> 06:53.140
﻿I don't want to!
I said, show it to me

07:05.490 --> 07:07.450
﻿The star-eyed knight...

07:13.450 --> 07:14.700
﻿Francis..

07:15.200 --> 07:16.700
﻿Please, notice me...!

07:17.370 --> 07:19.830
﻿Francis... Francis!

07:30.800 --> 07:31.550
﻿Nadja...

08:11.890 --> 08:13.050
﻿You can't sleep?

08:14.430 --> 08:15.220
﻿Yeah...

08:18.060 --> 08:19.430
﻿Why don't you keep me company?

08:31.610 --> 08:32.780
﻿Here you are.

08:33.240 --> 08:34.370
﻿Thank you.

08:37.200 --> 08:39.830
﻿Huh? Isn't that Master's wine...

08:40.330 --> 08:42.920
﻿When I can't sleep, I pilfer a little bit of it.

08:43.460 --> 08:44.080
﻿It's a secret, okay?

08:44.710 --> 08:45.250
﻿Okay.

08:47.460 --> 08:49.050
﻿He seems very nice, doesn't he?

08:50.300 --> 08:52.090
﻿He's your Francis, right?

08:56.100 --> 08:57.720
﻿You were able to see the person you love...

08:58.220 --> 09:00.180
﻿...but, you don't seem happy.

09:00.640 --> 09:02.190
﻿It's not that I'm not happy...

09:04.860 --> 09:05.610
﻿But...

09:06.440 --> 09:07.230
﻿But?

09:09.280 --> 09:10.070
﻿I'm afraid.

09:11.200 --> 09:12.570
﻿I want to go to him, but...

09:13.410 --> 09:14.610
﻿I want to talk to him, but...

09:15.280 --> 09:16.320
﻿...I can't.

09:17.410 --> 09:20.540
﻿I don't even know if he remembers me.

09:21.910 --> 09:23.460
﻿It terrifies me.

09:24.750 --> 09:26.830
﻿It's only natural to be uneasy.

09:29.590 --> 09:31.920
﻿You said to me...

09:32.470 --> 09:34.380
﻿"You want to see him, don't you?"

09:35.390 --> 09:38.550
﻿"If you can see him, you have to do it!"

10:27.310 --> 10:29.190
﻿Excuse me, this is Nadja!

10:30.360 --> 10:32.320
﻿Francis... um...

10:36.240 --> 10:37.410
﻿Francis...?

10:39.450 --> 10:41.370
﻿Where are you, Francis?

10:41.990 --> 10:43.200
﻿Why can't I see you?

10:43.540 --> 10:45.290
﻿You are so close to me, but...

10:46.120 --> 10:47.830
﻿...maybe, we'll just end up...

10:48.380 --> 10:49.670
﻿...going our separate ways.

10:50.500 --> 10:51.340
﻿No!

10:51.670 --> 10:54.130
That's not true! That's not true!

10:54.470 --> 10:55.630
﻿That's not...!

10:57.800 --> 10:59.010
﻿That's not...

11:03.430 --> 11:06.180
﻿Just what... am I doing?

11:26.790 --> 11:28.620
﻿It looks just like the tree at Applefield.

11:29.330 --> 11:31.040
﻿It reminds me of those days.

11:38.970 --> 11:40.380
﻿It's beautiful...

11:42.550 --> 11:43.720
﻿What a nice breeze.

11:56.360 --> 11:57.320
﻿Francis...!

12:18.880 --> 12:19.970
﻿Francis?

12:21.220 --> 12:23.720
﻿You sure are good at climbing trees, Nadja.

12:24.260 --> 12:26.760
﻿Ah! Uh, please wait a moment!

12:29.520 --> 12:30.560
﻿Be careful...

12:35.860 --> 12:36.940
﻿Are you okay?

12:38.070 --> 12:39.360
﻿I-I'm okay!

12:39.610 --> 12:41.030
﻿See? Look!

12:42.700 --> 12:43.870
﻿Thank goodness.

12:51.960 --> 12:53.370
﻿What am I going to do?

12:54.000 --> 12:55.420
﻿What am I going to say?

12:55.420 --> 12:57.880
﻿Uhhh... Ummm...

12:58.710 --> 13:02.340
﻿U-U-Uhhh... Why did you make a donation to the orphanage?

13:05.890 --> 13:07.600
﻿It's called a "noblesse oblige".

13:08.600 --> 13:10.180
﻿Noblesse oblige?

13:11.140 --> 13:13.730
﻿The obligation and responsibility demanded
of those born into high stature...

13:14.060 --> 13:15.520
﻿That's what it means.

13:16.690 --> 13:19.150
﻿My mother, who passed away, taught me that.

13:20.900 --> 13:23.740
﻿My mother, for the sake of children without a family...

13:23.990 --> 13:25.870
﻿...volunteered practically everyday.

13:26.370 --> 13:30.410
﻿She said, "When the children laugh, I feel happy, too."

13:31.540 --> 13:33.870
﻿To visit orphanages like that...

13:33.870 --> 13:35.210
﻿...or to make donations...

13:35.580 --> 13:37.920
﻿...is called the whim of an aristocrat by many, but...

13:38.460 --> 13:39.880
﻿As a human being, my mother...

13:39.880 --> 13:43.300
﻿...tried very hard to be of use to someone.

13:46.550 --> 13:48.970
﻿I want to help people, too.

13:49.930 --> 13:52.600
﻿That's why, I travel to different areas, collecting donations...

13:52.940 --> 13:55.230
﻿And, give that to the people who need it.

13:55.770 --> 13:59.480
﻿Because, I believe that's my "noblesse oblige."

14:01.900 --> 14:03.900
﻿Francis, you're really great...

14:04.740 --> 14:07.280
﻿I'm not doing anything special...

14:08.580 --> 14:11.910
﻿The noblesse oblige is... something anyone can do.

14:12.960 --> 14:14.120
﻿Anyone?

14:14.330 --> 14:15.000
﻿That's right.

14:16.040 --> 14:17.380
﻿Even if it's something very small...

14:17.670 --> 14:19.840
﻿If you can make someone happy..

14:20.590 --> 14:23.260
﻿That's what you call, the noblesse oblige.

14:29.890 --> 14:33.060
﻿So, what's my noblesse oblige?

14:34.060 --> 14:36.060
﻿I wonder if I have it in me, too?

14:36.440 --> 14:38.810
﻿Something I can do for someone...

14:38.900 --> 14:42.020
﻿How do you dance that? Please, teach me?

14:42.280 --> 14:43.940
﻿Like this, and this.

14:44.110 --> 14:45.780
﻿Like this, then this.

14:55.210 --> 14:57.080
﻿Right foot, left foot.

14:58.000 --> 14:59.460
﻿Turn, and...

14:59.840 --> 15:01.290
﻿Tap, tap, tap.

15:02.000 --> 15:05.460
﻿Turn, and clap.

15:06.050 --> 15:08.010
﻿That's right! Like that!

15:09.760 --> 15:12.430
﻿What's Nadja doing?

15:12.680 --> 15:15.770
﻿Ahhh! She's teaching them a dance.

15:16.270 --> 15:18.810
﻿Yesterday, there were kids who could dance and others who couldn't...

15:19.270 --> 15:22.570
﻿So, "I'm going to make it so everyone can dance!” she said.

15:22.940 --> 15:24.730
﻿That's just like Nadja.

15:36.250 --> 15:37.330
﻿iMr-. Francis! » -

15:39.330 --> 15:41.130
Dance with us too, Mr. Francis.

16:21.250 --> 16:22.170
﻿Everyone...

16:22.380 --> 16:24.540
﻿Let's get ready for dinner!

16:24.800 --> 16:26.130
﻿Yes, ma'am!!!

16:27.260 --> 16:28.710
﻿Dinner! Dinner!

16:29.050 --> 16:29.970
﻿Nadja!

16:30.220 --> 16:31.800
﻿Let's go help!

16:32.010 --> 16:32.550
﻿Okay!

16:33.720 --> 16:35.300
﻿I’ll see you later.

16:35.760 --> 16:36.350
﻿Okay..

16:37.270 --> 16:39.060
﻿Dinner! Dinner! Dinner! Dinner!

16:39.060 --> 16:41.310
﻿Geez, Kennosuke!

16:43.860 --> 16:46.400
I have news for all of you.

16:46.780 --> 16:50.690
﻿Mr. Francis will be leaving the Le Man Orphanage tomorrow.

16:54.030 --> 16:56.580
﻿I have to go to a hospital in Geneva.

16:57.120 --> 16:58.580
﻿It was a short time, but...

16:58.750 --> 16:59.500
﻿I enjoyed it.

17:00.410 --> 17:01.210
﻿Madam director!

17:01.580 --> 17:03.370
﻿We're leaving tomorrow as well.

17:03.750 --> 17:05.670
﻿Wait a minute, Master!

17:05.790 --> 17:07.170
﻿That's so sudden...!

17:07.380 --> 17:08.880
﻿We're traveling performers.

17:09.970 --> 17:11.840
﻿We cannot just stay in one place.

17:12.550 --> 17:13.590
﻿In the next town...

17:13.590 --> 17:17.050
﻿...there are people who are eagerly waiting for us, too.

17:19.430 --> 17:22.690
﻿Just when I got to be friends with everyone...

17:24.480 --> 17:25.810
Okay! Everyone!

17:26.650 --> 17:30.070
﻿If everyone is looking sad, they won't be able to leave happy.

17:30.900 --> 17:34.160
﻿Now, let's all have a nice meal tonight.

17:34.530 --> 17:36.120
﻿Yes, ma'am...

18:26.250 --> 18:27.330
﻿Francis!

18:30.000 --> 18:30.710
﻿Nadja...!

18:31.420 --> 18:32.420
﻿Please, wait there.

18:32.670 --> 18:33.760
﻿I'll be down in a...

18:36.840 --> 18:37.720
﻿Please, stay there.

18:42.270 --> 18:43.850
﻿You can't see anything, can you?

18:44.680 --> 18:45.230
﻿No.

18:45.940 --> 18:47.560
﻿I used to climb trees often.

18:49.110 --> 18:50.400
﻿You, too?

18:51.690 --> 18:53.940
﻿There was a large tree on our estate...

18:55.150 --> 18:56.320
﻿When you climb it...

18:56.700 --> 18:59.620
﻿...the familiar scenery looks a little different.

19:00.330 --> 19:04.120
﻿I used to climb a large apple tree at the orphanage.

19:05.040 --> 19:07.000
﻿You could see so far...

19:07.120 --> 19:09.630
﻿When I saw that, somehow it would cheer me up.

19:10.090 --> 19:11.880
﻿Yes, I understand that.

19:12.750 --> 19:15.880
﻿When you're feeling down, you can look at the wide landscape...

19:16.470 --> 19:18.880
﻿...and it makes your worries seem really small.

19:19.550 --> 19:21.430
﻿Yes... and it's fun too.

19:22.220 --> 19:25.140
﻿I wonder what kind of town is over that hill.

19:25.680 --> 19:28.730
﻿What kind of people live there... that's what I would imagine.

19:29.810 --> 19:31.020
﻿And, you think to yourself...

19:31.940 --> 19:34.150
﻿Someday, I'm going there!

19:37.820 --> 19:39.530
﻿We're kind of alike, aren't we?

19:39.990 --> 19:40.780
﻿Yes, we are.

19:42.580 --> 19:44.030
﻿Noblesse oblige...

19:44.620 --> 19:46.330
﻿Did I do it?

19:48.120 --> 19:51.580
﻿I thought of doing something for others just like you, Francis.

19:53.170 --> 19:55.880
﻿If the children here could dance and have fun...

19:56.210 --> 19:58.130
﻿I thought they might like it.

19:59.510 --> 20:00.300
﻿Nadja...

20:02.680 --> 20:04.640
﻿The children were so enthusiastic...

20:04.760 --> 20:06.350
﻿...and really having fun.

20:09.060 --> 20:11.350
﻿You made everyone smile.

20:14.020 --> 20:15.320
﻿If that's true..

20:16.820 --> 20:17.570
﻿I'm glad.

20:24.330 --> 20:25.450
It's dawn.

20:26.290 --> 20:27.120
﻿Yes...

20:31.370 --> 20:32.250
﻿Francis..

20:32.750 --> 20:34.420
﻿Take care of yourself...

20:35.800 --> 20:38.710
﻿It's wonderful that you help others, but...

20:39.420 --> 20:42.220
﻿If you're not all right, everyone will worry.

20:43.640 --> 20:44.180
﻿Okay.

20:45.760 --> 20:46.560
﻿And...

20:48.270 --> 20:49.930
Please, don't work too hard.

20:50.940 --> 20:54.190
﻿That's because, there are a lot of people who are waiting for you.

20:55.520 --> 20:56.150
Okay.

20:57.030 --> 20:57.900
﻿And...

20:58.570 --> 20:59.320
﻿And...

21:01.700 --> 21:02.570
﻿And?

21:04.370 --> 21:05.370
﻿And...

21:07.490 --> 21:10.000
﻿We'll see each other again, won't we?

21:12.000 --> 21:12.790
﻿Yes, we will.

21:14.380 --> 21:16.250
﻿We'll definitely... see each other again.

22:15.370 --> 22:18.620
Paris is sunnier than London

22:15.370 --> 22:18.620
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

22:18.740 --> 22:21.830
Carmen likes paella more than pasta

22:18.740 --> 22:21.830
CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

22:22.250 --> 22:28.420
The Queen of Spades is a fickle person

22:22.250 --> 22:28.420
SUPEEDO no jou kimagure yasan

22:29.380 --> 22:30.620
Indeed

22:29.380 --> 22:30.620
Kitto

22:33.380 --> 22:35.800
It's not use worrying about it

22:33.380 --> 22:35.800
Nayan datte MUDA yo

22:36.380 --> 22:39.510
Que sera sera, sera Sera

22:36.380 --> 22:39.510
KE SERA SERA SERA SERA

22:39.770 --> 22:44.480
Tomorrow's going to be whatever it was meant

22:39.770 --> 22:44.480
Ashita nante itsumo naru you ni

22:44.560 --> 22:45.940
To be, to be

22:44.560 --> 22:45.940
Naru naru

22:46.270 --> 22:51.280
The tree fog won

22:46.270 --> 22:51.280
Sekai KAERU tobi KONKUURU

22:51.740 --> 22:55.660
The world frog-jumping contest

22:51.740 --> 22:55.660
Yuushou shita yo AMAGAERU

22:58.870 --> 23:05.040
Under the kitten's paw

22:58.870 --> 23:05.040
Koneko chan no ashi no ura wa

23:05.460 --> 23:11.630
Is the scent of the sun, right?

23:05.460 --> 23:11.630
Otentou sama no nioi dane

23:14.470 --> 23:17.800
Paris is sunnier than London

23:14.470 --> 23:17.800
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

23:17.890 --> 23:20.890
Carmen likes paella more than pasta

23:17.890 --> 23:20.890
CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

